    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0186" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/>

                <head>No. 41.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Phelps</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 27,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have read with pleasure your No. 6, of
                    the 2d instant, relative to the restrictions upon the importation of American
                    pork into Austria-Hungary. Your representations thereon appear to have been
                    energetic and discreet, and are approved, as reflecting the views of this
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
